],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"The highest heavens belong to the LORD, but the earth He has given to mankind.","verse":16},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"It is not the dead who praise the LORD, nor any who descend into silence.","verse":17},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"LORD","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord"},"text":"But it is we who will bless the LORD, both now and forevermore. Hallelujah!","verse":18}],"id":"Lord","label":"LORD","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Lord::LORD::reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","scope":"reviewed_capitalized_divine_title","senseReview":"Only literal uppercase LORD is admitted globally. Source Lord article explicitly covers God as Lord; lowercase human lord and sentence-title Lord are not inferred from this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Lord","term":"LORD"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Lord","sourceTitle":"Lord"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.111.1-117.2","r":"Ps.111.1-117.2","rawR":"Ps.111.1-117.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.111.1-117.2","value":"Ps.111.1-117.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 111–117"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The refrain ",{"c":["Praise the"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"},{"c":["!"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (Hebrew ",{"c":["haleluyah"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},") characterizes this group of psalms."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.111.1-117.2","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":117,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":111,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.111.1-117.2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[111,112,113,114,115,116,117],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"22b6425eac56925667128161925e7981d1b2aac4109f6fbee20150584747df92","sourceItemName":"Ps.111.1-117.2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7176,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.111.1-117.2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.111.1-117.2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.113.1-118.29","r":"Ps.113.1-118.29","rawR":"Ps.113.1-118.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.113.1-118.29","value":"Ps.113.1-118.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 113–118"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," These psalms form what is known as the “Egyptian Hallel” (",{"c":["hallel"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," means “praise”) because Jews use the collection in the celebration of Passover, which was instituted at the beginning of the exodus from Egypt. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.113.1-114.8","r":"Ps.113.1-114.8","rawR":"Ps.113.1-114.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.113.1-114.8","value":"Ps.113.1-114.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Psalms 113–114"}," are recited before the Passover meal and ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.115.1-118.29","r":"Ps.115.1-118.29","rawR":"Ps.115.1-118.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.115.1-118.29","value":"Ps.115.1-118.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Pss 115–118"}," afterward."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.113.1-118.29","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":118,"endVerse":29,"startChapter":113,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.113.1-118.29","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[113,114,115,116,117,118],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3bb66210be6b57d7effeab71c9a1a99f778790f8fc5109e3183b8ed871025210","sourceItemName":"Ps.113.1-118.29","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7191,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.113.1-118.29","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.113.1-118.29","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.115.1-18","r":"Ps.115.1-18","rawR":"Ps.115.1-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.115.1-18","value":"Ps.115.1-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 115"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," In this hymn of thanksgiving for God’s blessings, the community ascribes all glory to the name of the Lord, who is the true source of hope and blessing. Meanwhile, those who trust in idols are greatly disappointed. The blessing of the Creator of heaven and earth extends to future generations (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.115.14","r":"Ps.115.14","rawR":"Ps.115.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.115.14","value":"Ps.115.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"115:14"},"), and especially to the priesthood (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.115.12","r":"Ps.115.12","rawR":"Ps.115.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.115.12","value":"Ps.115.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"115:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.115.1-18","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":115,"endVerse":18,"startChapter":115,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.115.1-18","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[115],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4abf2af81e4493e8cd2dc5bc864ec7faea6f4f6565df113d43c0f8e5b2baeeb6","sourceItemName":"Ps.115.1-18","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7203,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.115.1-18","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.115.1-18","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.115.1-3","r":"Ps.115.1-3","rawR":"Ps.115.1-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.115.1-3","value":"Ps.115.1-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"115:1-3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The community confesses their faith that God will rescue them for the glory of his name."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.115.1-3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":115,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":115,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.115.1-3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[115],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"ce26db110b3b726c02e78ab52d1ea19a45d6fa1da918237ee383d8374c695bf9","sourceItemName":"Ps.115.1-3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7204,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.115.1-3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.115.1-3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Ps.115.2-3","r":"Ps.115.2-3","rawR":"Ps.115.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.115.2-3","value":"Ps.115.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"115:2-3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Where is their God?"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," People deny God’s presence or power when he does not act as they think he should (cp. ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.14.1","r":"Ps.14.1","rawR":"Ps.14.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.14.1","value":"Ps.14.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.3","r":"Ps.42.3","rawR":"Ps.42.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.3","value":"Ps.42.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"42:3"},", ",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.10","r":"Ps.42.10","rawR":"Ps.42.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.10","value":"Ps.42.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"10"},"). However, ",{"c":["God is in the heavens"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},"—he has all power, authority, and knowledge. He ",{"c":["does as he wishes"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," not what people think he should do. He works out his plans in accord with his will (",{"href":"?bref=Eph.1.11","r":"Eph.1.11","rawR":"Eph.1.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Eph.1.11","value":"Eph.1.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Eph 1:11"},") and acts in his own time and in ways he chooses."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Ps.115.2-3","refs":[{"book":"PSA","endChapter":115,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":115,"startVerse":2}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ps.115.2-3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"PSA","sourceChapterCoverage":[115],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2fb07cb672186547bb902440402aa0a7c7264baf39715f542a8c784bd4cd2ab2","sourceItemName":"Ps.115.2-3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":7205,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"PSA","canonicalOSIS":"Ps","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Ps"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Ps.115.2-3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Ps.115.2-3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"hre